  "summary": "WIRED reports that more than 150 Motorola ALPR cameras were misconfigured to expose live video feeds and vehicle data\u2014including plates, makes, and models\u2014to the open internet without authentication. Security researcher Matt Brown discovered the flaw after reverse-engineering a camera bought on eBay; Motorola confirmed the exposure and said it is working with customers and pushing a firmware update.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "More than 150 Motorola ALPR cameras have exposed their video feeds and leaking data in recent months",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "By leaving these incredibly insecure tracking devices on the open internet, police have not only breached public trust but created a bounty of location data for everyone who drives by which can be abused by stalkers and other criminals",
      "paragraph_idx": 24
    },
    {
      "quote": "Some customer-modified network configurations potentially exposed certain IP addresses",
